{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":291,"output":2542,"cacheRead":16896,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1110,"totalTokens":19729,"cost":{"input":0.000873,"output":0.038130000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0050688,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0440718}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The full flow works:\n1. Intro page with Continue button ✓\n2. Non-empty display name (empty rejected with \"This field is required.\") ✓\n3. Final page includes submitted name ✓\n4. Exports benchmark-study ✓\n5. Uploads via raco congame upload ✓\n\nNow write exercise.rkt that automates this flow using net/url with cookie handling, so `racket exercise.rkt` verifies everything. I'll implement a small client: cookie jar, GET with redirect following (manually, since net/url doesn't follow redirects automatically; also Location may be relative), form parsing for the action URL, and multipart POST.\n\nnet/url supports POST via post-impure-port with data — I need multipart/form-data body. I can construct it manually.\n\nLet me write exercise.rkt:\n\n- jar: hash of cookie name -> value (just for host.docker.internal path /).\n- http-req: function taking method, url, optional body/content-type, returns status, headers, body bytes.\n- Follow 302 manually up to N times.\n- Parse href/action via regexp.\n\nSteps:\n1. GET anon-login URL → expect 200, page has /study/<slug> link (the \"Redirecting...\" page). Actually curl -L followed to study page? Earlier -L gave \"Redirecting...\" page with meta refresh href to /study/slug. It returned 200 with meta refresh. So parse the href to /study/....\n2. GET study page → expect h1 \"Welcome\", extract Continue href.\n3. Follow Continue (follow redirects) → expect form with input name=\"name\" and action.\n4. POST empty name → expect 200 page with \"This field is required.\"\n5. Re-extract action from error page, POST name=\"Exercise Tester\" → follow redirect → expect final page containing \"Exercise Tester\" and \"Thank You\".\n\nCookie handling: parse Set-Cookie headers, simple: take first name=value pair, ignore attributes. Store in hash.\n\nnet/url's get-impure-port/head+impure-port... For POST: post-impure-port url post-data [headers]. It doesn't follow redirects (raises or returns?). net/url follows redirects? http-conn? Simpler to use net/http-client? http-client doesn't do cookies either, but it returns status and headers and does NOT follow redirects — good for manual control. Use net/http-client: http-conn, http-conn-sendrecv!\n\nLet me write it with net/http-client:\n\n```racket\n(require net/http-client racket/string racket/port)\n\n(define host \"host.docker.internal\")\n(define port 46639)\n(define slug \"bench-20260827t105820z-smoke--1aa51d42\")\n\n(define cookies (make-hash)) ; name -> value\n\n(define (cookie-header)\n  (string-join (hash-map cookies (λ (k v) (format \"~a=~a\" k v))) \"; \"))\n\n(define (store-cookies! headers)\n  (for ([h (in-list headers)])\n    (match h\n      [(pregexp #rx\"(?i:^set-cookie: *([^=;]+)=([^;]*))\" (list _ n v))\n       (hash-set! cookies n v)]\n      [_ (void)])))\n\n(define (request method path [body #f] [ctype #f])\n  (define conn (http-conn-open host #:port port #:ssl? #f))\n  (define headers\n    (append\n     (if (zero? (hash-count cookies)) '() (list (format \"Cookie: ~a\" (cookie-header))))\n     (if ctype (list (format \"Content-Type: ~a\" ctype)) '())))\n  (define-values (status resp-headers in)\n    (http-conn-sendrecv! conn path #:method method\n                         #:headers headers\n                         #:data (or body #\"\") ; hmm, only for POST\n                         ))\n  ...)\n```\n\nhttp-conn-sendrecv! signature: (http-conn-sendrecv! conn uri [#:version ... #:method method #:headers headers #:data data #:content-length ...]). data is bytes/string for PUT/POST.\n\nReturn status line string, headers list of strings? http-conn-sendrecv! returns (values status-line headers-list port) where headers-list is list of bytes? Let me just convert bytes->string.\n\nRedirect following: if status starts with \"302\" or \"301\", find Location header (may be relative path), recurse.\n\nMultipart body:\n\n```racket\n(define (multipart-body fields)\n  (define boundary \"----exercise-boundary-1234\")\n  (define parts\n    (apply bytes-append\n     (for/list ([(k v) (in-dict fields)])\n       (bytes-append\n        (string->bytes/utf-8\n         (format \"--~a\\r\\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\\\"~a\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n~a\\r\\n\" boundary k v))))))\n  (values (bytes-append parts (string->bytes/utf-8 (format \"--~a--\\r\\n\" boundary)))\n          (format \"multipart/form-data; boundary=~a\" boundary)))\n```\n\nThen checks with error reporting. Write exercise.rkt and run it.\n\nOne concern: anon-login creates a new participant each time, which is fine for exercise.\n\nLet me write it."}}
