html{@h1{Hi @|name|!}\n\n        Do you consent?\n\n        @button[accepted]{Yes}\n        @button[rejected]{No}})\n\n(defstep (consented)\n  @html{You consented. @button{Continue}})\n\n(defstep (didnt-consent)\n  @html{You didn't consent. @button{Continue}})\n\n(defstep (done)\n  @html{Thanks! You're done.})\n\n(defstudy consent\n  #:requires (name)\n  #:provides (consented?)\n  [give-consent --> ,(λ () (if consented? 'consented 'didnt-consent))]\n  [consented --> ,done]\n  [didnt-consent --> ,done])\n\n(defstudy example\n  [info --> tell-name --> consent --> done])\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787828325986},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"bash_5","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"614:representation. Keyword arguments specifically noted above are required for their respective\n689:more @secref[\"validators\" #:doc '(lib \"forms/forms.scrbl\")].\n697:    [my-name (ensure binding/text (required))]\n699:    [my-age (ensure binding/number (required))]))\n754:   (required)\n799:@defproc[(required-unless [pred (-> any/c)])\n804:Similar to @racket[required], produces a validator procedure that ensures a value is present (i.e.\n815:Produces a validator procedure that ensures a numeric value is greater than or equal to\n833:Produces a validator procedure that ensures a numeric value falls within the range\n852:Produces a validator procedure that ensures a value is a non-empty list containing at least\n853:@racket[n] items. Unlike @racket[at-least] and @racket[number-in-range], this validator\n892:     [choice (ensure binding/text (required) (one-of choices))]))\n980:validation messages (such as \"This field is required\") in a single location.\n1153:Returns a validator procedure that checks if a form field's value equals @racket[_expected].\n1165:        #:validators (list (is-equal \"c\" #:message \"That's not correct, try again!\")))\n1173:                                   [#:n num-required exact-nonnegative-integer? 0]\n1182:@racket[_num-requi