ired))]\n     [checkbox-choices (ensure binding/list (list-of choice-formlet))]\n     [radio-choice     (ensure choice-formlet (required))]\n     [select-choice    (ensure choice-formlet (required))]))\n\n  (define (render rw)\n    @md*{@rw[\"name\" @input-text{Enter your name}]   ; Customized label\n         @rw[\"age\" (input-number)]\n         @rw[\"checkbox-choices\" (checkboxes choices)]\n         @rw[\"radio-choice\" (radios choices)]\n         @rw[\"select-choice\" (select (cons '(\"\" . \"Please select something\") choices) \"\")]\n         @|submit-button|})\n\n  @md{# Survey\n\n      @form[survey-form on-submit render]})\n\n(defstep (display-info)\n  @md{# Thanks\n\n      * Name: @name\n      * Age: @~a[age]\n      * Checkbox choices: @(string-join checkbox-choices \", \")\n      * Radio choice: @radio-choice\n      * Select choice: @select-choice})\n\n(defstudy example-form-study\n  [intro --> survey --> display-info --> ,(λ () done)])\n}|\n\n\n@;===============================================\n\n@section{Multi-participant Study Recipe}\n\n@inline-note{See a @secref[\"multi-participant-tutorial\"] to learn how this study works.}\n\n@codeblock|{\n#lang conscript\n\n(require conscript/form0\n         conscript/survey-tools\n         racket/list)\n\n(provide simple-treatment-study)\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; TREATMENT ASSIGNMENT\n;; =============================================================================\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787828441957},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have everything I need. Write study.rkt:\n\n```racket\n#lang conscript\n\n(require conscript/form0)\n\n(provide benchmark-study)\n\n(defvar name)\n\n(defstep (intro)\n  @html{@h1{Welcome}\n        Welcome to this short study.\n        @button{Continue}})\n\n(defstep (ask-name)\n  (define-values (name-form on-submit)\n    (form+submit\n     [name (ensure binding/text (required))]))\n  (define (render rw)\n    @html*{...})\n  ...\n```\n\nSince binding/text produces #f for empty strings, `(required)` suffices for non-empty. Good.\n\nRender with @html or @md*. The cookbook uses @md* with @rw. I'll use @html-ish. Note conscript provides `html` and `html*`. Let me write:\n\n```racket\n(defstep (ask-name)\n  (define-values (name-form on-submit)\n    (form+submit\n     [name (ensure binding/text (required))]))\n\n  (define (render rw)\n    @md*{@rw[\"name\" @input-text{Display name:}]\n         @|submit-button|})\n\n  @md{# What is your name?\n\n      @form[name-form on-submit render]})\n\n(defstep (done)\n  @md{# Thank you, @|name|!\n\n      Your display name is: **@|name|**.})\n\n(defstudy benchmark-study\n  [intro --> ask-name --> done --> ,(λ () done)])\n```\n\nHmm, final transition: `[done --> done]` like examples. Actually kitchen-sink uses `[done --> done]`? form.rkt uses `[done --> done]`. Use that.\n\nCheck whether `form+submit` needs `conscript/form0` require — yes per docs. Note the task mentions \"generated-binding warnings in the current Conscript review extension\" for the fixture — probably fine.\n\nAlso input-text with label: `@rw[\"name\" @input-text{Enter your name}]`.\n\nNow also exercise.rkt to exercise against the server. The participant URL is `_anon-login/<slug>`. I could write a script that uses net/url to log in anonymously, follow steps, submit a name, verify final page contains name, and also test empty name rejection. Need cookie handling. Check if there's an example exercise in reference. Let me check congame-doc for a testing how-to, or check examples dir. Maybe simpler: write exercise.rkt using net/url and net/cookie? Racket has net/cookie collection. Let me write it.\n\nFirst compile and upload the study, then test manually with curl, then write exercise.rkt.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" I\",\"format\"